        <chapter title="4. Create a Lifecycle Class" id="4-create-a-lifecycle-class">
            <p>Lifecycle classes allow you to execute code during plugin lifecycle events. Your lifecycle class must
                implement <code>PluginLifecycle</code>.</p>

            <p>Just like Paper plugins, it can (but isn't required to) define <code>onLoad</code>, <code>onEnable</code>,
